  "description": "EARLY - not ready for real work yet.\n\n      Moves NetTopologySuite geometry from one coordinate reference system to another with PROJ,\n      the engine every GIS uses. Reproject reads the CRS a geometry is in from its SRID and moves\n      it to another EPSG code, saying how accurate that is and warning when coordinates lie\n      outside where a CRS is meant to be used. CRS says what an EPSG code is: name, units, area\n      of use. Longitude comes first, always.\n\n      PROJ 9.5.1 and its EPSG database come bundled (through SharpProj), so nothing else needs\n      installing. Windows x64 only, as vvvv gamma is. Requires the Visual C++ 2015-2022 runtime,\n      which most Windows machines have.\n\n      Requires vvvv gamma 7.2 or newer (.NET 8).",
  "id": "VL.PROJ",
  "isPrerelease": true,
  "lastEdited": "2026-11-14T07:33:06.617Z",
