  "readmeFile": "docs\\README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.0.1-alpha (2026-11-14) - First release. Two nodes in category PROJ. Reproject moves a\n      NetTopologySuite geometry from the CRS its SRID names to another EPSG code, and says how\n      accurate that is and whether coordinates lie outside where a CRS is meant to be used. CRS says\n      what an EPSG code is: name, units, area of use. PROJ 9.5.1 and its EPSG database are bundled.\n      With VL.PROJ installed, VL.NetTopologySuite's GeometryEditor window and drawn Geometry IOBox\n      name any EPSG code. Requires VL.NetTopologySuite 0.0.7-alpha. Help patches: HowTo Move a\n      geometry to another CRS, HowTo Look up a CRS.",
  "requireLicenseAcceptance": false,
  "summary": "PROJ coordinate transformation for VL.NetTopologySuite, as nodes for vvvv gamma.",
  "title": "VL.PROJ - coordinate transformation for NetTopologySuite in vvvv gamma",
